	)
	(text "NOTES\n1. Burn path: VBAT_SADS -> Q401 (ARM) -> J401/J402 -> Q403/Q404 (FIRE) -> GND. Needs ARM and FIRE both on.\n2. SADS-EN-1 = ARM, SADS-EN-2 = FIRE 1, SADS-EN-3 = FIRE 2. Burn timing in FW, one channel at a time.\n3. 4.7k gate pulldowns hold all FETs off during RP2350 reset (E9). PCS R19/R20/R22 duplicate these, TBD w/ Rohan.\n4. Burn wire R / current TBD (bench test). Keep under ~3 A.\n5. J401/J402 footprint TBD w/ structures. VBAT_SADS rail TBD (VBAT_RAW or VLSA ch)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.46 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "bbb11830-0ae9-48ee-a182-5a3620a44d81")
	)
	(text "CALCS\nQ401 VGS = -VBAT x 100k/147k: -5.7 V @ 8.4 V, -4.1 V @ 6.0 V\n  DMG2305UXQ VGS max +/-8 V. Divider draws 57 uA armed, 0 safe.\nFIRE gate = 3.3 V x 4.7k/4.8k = 3.23 V (DMG3420UQ spec'd @ 2.5 V)\nQ403/Q404 @ 3.3 A: 3.3^2 x 48m = 0.52 W (PD max 0.74 W)\nGPIO high: 3.3 V / 4.7k = 0.7 mA per line\nBoth burn points at once ~6.6 A -> never fire both"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 36.83 128.27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c0fdf124-e85a-4a35-8065-75bda35c5d0e")
	)
